{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790724775,"nonce":"7Qg38VAhg59aNUXjL+Aoef3K1Wo=","title":"Interpreter-first tiering cannot use the outlined OSR path for a loop in a function that returns an aggregate through a hidden destination pointer.","message":"`osr::outline` rejects every layout with a destination even though `OsrLayout` already reserves a frame slot for it and the Cranelift resume adapter knows how to restore it. The LLVM fallback helper rejects the same layout. Tiering therefore falls back to the unoptimised whole-function helper or fails to promote the outlined region.\n\nObserved on the NUC with the Lua `any_field` kernel and static-hot compilation disabled to exercise interpreter loop OSR: the baseline reports `region not outlined`, and LLVM reports `OSR helper for a destination return`. The checksum remains correct through the Cranelift fallback, but the timed body takes about 18 ms.\n\nTeach both paths to restore the destination from the OSR frame, retain the destination in the outlined adapter layout, and cover outlining plus LLVM verification with destination-return regression tests.\n\nParent: 590ec28d7786718e0662b78308836ee435a00d6dc384ce2418ad09ac099b97d2","files":null}]}